{%- doc -%}
  The product's name in the language being viewed.

  This just echoes `product.title`, because Shopify's translation layer already
  returns the right language: the item master's Arabic is registered as the `ar`
  translation of every product (by the elixir-translations tool), so `/ar` gets
  Arabic and `/` gets English with nothing to do here.

  It deliberately does NOT read `custom.arabic_name`. That metafield is the SOURCE
  the translations are built from, not something to render. Metafields are
  themselves translatable, and an `ar` translation registered against
  `custom.arabic_name` by another app made this snippet emit a stale English name
  on Arabic pages while `product.title` had been correct all along.

  Kept as a snippet so every product name on the storefront still has one place to
  change.

  @param {object} product - the product
  @param {boolean} [escape] - escape the output for use in an attribute

  Usage:
    {%- render 'elx-product-title', product: product -%}
    alt="{%- render 'elx-product-title', product: product, escape: true -%}"
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  if escape
    echo product.title | escape
  else
    echo product.title
  endif
-%}
